      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: As a separate minor issue (pre-existing but worth noting): if a timer is scheduled exactly at the microsecond when the lower 32 bits wrap around (`deadline \u003d\u003d 0`), `evt_expired_us` becomes `0`. \n\nSince `0` is used as a sentinel for \"no events scheduled\" (e.g., set in `__hw_clock_event_clear`), `__hw_clock_event_irq` might inadvertently overwrite this valid timer with `EVT_MAX_EXPIRED_US` if `CONFIG_LOW_POWER_IDLE` is enabled. \n\nUsing a separate boolean flag for event validity (e.g. `evt_is_set`) instead of overloading `0` would prevent this rare (~every 71.58 minutes) edge case.",
